What this licence does and does not cover
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

It covers what is in this repository: the four libraries and the two binaries
(`Sources/` — AII, Seam, Sewn, Thread; AIIServer and AIICLI), their tests
(`Tests/`), the protocol definitions (`Protos/`), the example app
(`Examples/Notes`), the scripts and the documentation under `Docs/`. Parts of
it came from Conduit (Apache-2.0 at the time, relicensed here by its copyright
holder), Sewn and Thread (GPL-3).

It does not cover what a build pulls in. AII resolves its dependencies at build
time and redistributes none of them here; each keeps its own licence. The
direct ones — grpc-swift and its NIO transport and protobuf plugins,
swift-protobuf, swift-log, swift-crypto, swift-argument-parser, hummingbird and
hummingbird-websocket, swift-prometheus, supabase-swift — are Apache-2.0 or
MIT; Web3.swift is MIT.

Frigate (https://github.com/rao-studios/Frigate) is the one dependency behind
the `Server` trait that is ours, resolved at build time like the rest, not
vendored. It is MIT, except its `SinatraHarness` product and `sinatra-harness`
command, which are GPL-3.0-only (Frigate's NOTICE and
`Sources/SinatraHarness/LICENSE`). Frigate carries the MLX stack used for
on-device inference, embeddings and graph extraction; its SinatraHarness
product carries the on-device harness Sewn's `local` provider runs through.
Until 2026-10 that product was its own repository
(github.com/riteshpakala/SinatraHarness, archived).

